    LLM: 'Game: 51. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '51 is a point-collection card game played in China and Japan. Players collect cards of the same suit; A-K-Q-J-10 of one suit scores 51 points. Chinese version: draw, discard, exchange; first to 500+ wins. Japanese version: pick board cards, discard; call "Stop!" with best hand; highest single-suit total wins.',
    objective: 'Chinese 51: Be first to 500+ points by making hands of five cards in one suit (A=11, K/Q/J=10, numeric=face). Japanese 51: Have the highest-scoring hand; sum best suit then subtract other suits; call "Stop!" when satisfied.',
    gameplay: 'Chinese: draw and discard, exchange cards; make hands of five in one suit (51 max). Japanese: pick from board, discard; call Stop when satisfied; best single-suit total wins (other suits subtract).',
